# Windsurf Rules for {{projectName}}

## Architecture: {{pattern}}
Components are under `{{basePath}}/`.

{{#if (eq pattern "atomic")}}
**Atomic Design layers:**
- `atoms/` → smallest: Button, Input, Icon
- `molecules/` → composed: SearchBar, FormField
- `organisms/` → complex: Navbar, ProductCard
- `templates/` → layouts
- `pages/` → routes
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq pattern "pages-components")}}
**Structure:**
- `{{basePath}}/components/` → reusable UI
- `{{basePath}}/pages/` → route pages
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq pattern "feature-first")}}
**Feature structure:**
- `{{basePath}}/features/<name>/` with `components/`, `hooks/`, `utils/`, `index.ts`
- `{{basePath}}/shared/` for cross-feature components
{{/if}}

## Naming Rules
- Component directories and files: `PascalCase`
- Each component in its own directory
- `index.ts` re-export in every component directory

## Standard Component Shape
```tsx
import React from 'react';
{{#if separateCss}}import styles from './ComponentName.module.css';{{/if}}

interface ComponentNameProps {
  children?: React.ReactNode;
}

export const ComponentName: React.FC<ComponentNameProps> = ({ children }) => {
  return <div{{#if separateCss}} className={styles.container}{{/if}}>{children}</div>;
};
```

```ts
// index.ts
export { ComponentName } from './ComponentName';
```

## Key Constraints
- No `export default` — use named exports
- No `any` types
- CSS Modules only{{#unless separateCss}} (disabled for this project){{/unless}}
- Tests with `@testing-library/react`{{#unless includeTests}} (disabled for this project){{/unless}}
